Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: Prefer exact PCI bus matches in VFCT

A relaxed match against an early VFCT entry can hide a later exact match
when multiple GPUs have the same vendor, device, slot, and function IDs.
On a MacPro6,1 with two FirePro D700 GPUs, this loads the bus-2 XA VBIOS
for the bus-6 GPU even though its distinct XB image is present.

Scan every entry for an exact PCI bus match before allowing the existing
fallback for platforms whose PCI buses were renumbered.

Validated the production selection functions against the machine's VFCT:
both GPU identities, reversed entry order, unmatched device IDs, and the
existing renumbered-bus fallback.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_bios.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_bios.c
@@ -376,19 +376,20 @@
  * amdgpu_acpi_vfct_match() - Check if a VFCT entry matches the device
  * @adev: AMDGPU device
  * @vhdr: VFCT image header to check
+ * @allow_bus_mismatch: Allow a relaxed match after checking all exact matches
  *
  * VFCT entries contain the PCI bus number as recorded during BIOS POST.
  * On systems where the kernel renumbers PCI buses (e.g. pci=realloc or
  * resource conflicts), the runtime bus number may differ from the POST
  * value.  Match by device identity (vendor + device + function) and use
- * the bus number as a preference: exact bus match is preferred, but when
- * the bus numbers disagree we accept the entry if the device identity
- * matches.
+ * the bus number as a preference. The caller first checks every entry for
+ * an exact match, then permits a relaxed match if none was found.
  *
  * Returns: 0 on match, -ENODEV on no match
  */
 static int amdgpu_acpi_vfct_match(struct amdgpu_device *adev,
-				  VFCT_IMAGE_HEADER *vhdr)
+				  VFCT_IMAGE_HEADER *vhdr,
+				  bool allow_bus_mismatch)
 {
 	/* Vendor and device IDs must always match */
 	if (vhdr->VendorID != adev->pdev->vendor ||
@@ -402,6 +403,8 @@
 	/* Exact bus number match - preferred */
 	if (vhdr->PCIBus == adev->pdev->bus->number)
 		return 0;
+	if (!allow_bus_mismatch)
+		return -ENODEV;
 
 	/* Bus mismatch but device identity matches (PCI renumbering case) */
 	dev_notice(adev->dev,
@@ -418,6 +421,7 @@
 	UEFI_ACPI_VFCT *vfct;
 	unsigned int offset;
 	bool r = false;
+	bool allow_bus_mismatch = false;
 
 	if (!ACPI_SUCCESS(acpi_get_table("VFCT", 1, &hdr)))
 		return false;
@@ -428,6 +432,7 @@
 	}
 
 	vfct = (UEFI_ACPI_VFCT *)hdr;
+retry:
 	offset = vfct->VBIOSImageOffset;
 
 	while (offset < tbl_size) {
@@ -447,7 +452,7 @@
 		}
 
 		if (vhdr->ImageLength &&
-		    !amdgpu_acpi_vfct_match(adev, vhdr)) {
+		    !amdgpu_acpi_vfct_match(adev, vhdr, allow_bus_mismatch)) {
 			adev->bios = kmemdup(&vbios->VbiosContent,
 					     vhdr->ImageLength,
 					     GFP_KERNEL);
@@ -462,6 +467,12 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/* Do not let an early relaxed match hide a later exact match. */
+	if (!allow_bus_mismatch) {
+		allow_bus_mismatch = true;
+		goto retry;
+	}
+
 	dev_info(adev->dev, "ACPI VFCT table present but broken (too short #2),skipping\n");
 
 out:
